{"entryId":"3150","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3150:1","sourceSha256":"d328714d63f8cfc47b6b912886d477f80b3556677e87484b4c1b577d76a0cdf0","englishSha256":"0bd544c5c98c7a2efcb76a610b58660f1cb8da9f933eeb6a0dd1f4915ba3f4c5","citations":[{"id":"3150:1:link-001","he":[29,43],"en":[65,76],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_71b.14"},"reference":"Yevamot 71b:14","assessment":"The witness reads Rabbah bar Yitzhak in Rav’s name.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 71b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_71b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3150:1:link-002","he":[44,58],"en":[78,88],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_45b.6"},"reference":"Chullin 45b:6","assessment":"The witness reads Rabbah bar Yitzhak in Rav’s name.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 45b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_45b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3150:1:link-003","he":[59,71],"en":[90,104],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_77a.2"},"reference":"Bava Batra 77a:2","assessment":"Bava Batra has Rabbah in Rav’s name for the two-documents rule.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 77a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_77a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3150:1:link-004","he":[72,107],"en":[106,161],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_27a.2"},"reference":"Kiddushin 27a:2","assessment":"The parallel two-documents rule reads Rava bar Yitzhak in Rav’s name. The father’s additional Rav title belongs to Heilprin.","evidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 27a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_27a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3150:1:link-005","he":[109,181],"en":[313,324],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_26b.11"},"reference":"Menachot 26b:11","assessment":"Menahot names Rav Yehudah opening the explanation, agreeing with Heilprin’s preferred title. Identity and reading of the cited new edition still require collation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 26b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_26b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3150:1:link-006","he":[183,209],"en":[326,368],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_55a.8"},"reference":"Avodah Zarah 55a:8","assessment":"The checked passage reads Rava addressing Rav Yehudah.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 55a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_55a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3150:1:link-007","he":[211,274],"en":[369,470],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_46b.14"},"reference":"Sotah 46b:14","assessment":"The rescuer, distance and result are exact, with the full passage speaking of the accompaniment in a town.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 46b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_46b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3150:1:link-008","he":[288,366],"en":[483,497],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_91a.10"},"reference":"Bava Batra 91a:10","assessment":"Verified Bavli reading is Huna. Heilprin names Ein Yaakov for the Yitzhak variant, also at 3139. No checked Ein Yaakov witness yet identifies this variant at the same locus.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 91a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_91a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 3139:1","target":{"entry":3139,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3150:1:link-009","he":[326,366],"en":[588,598],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ein_Yaakov_%28Glick_Edition%29%2C_Bava_Batra_5.38"},"reference":"Ein Yaakov (Glick Edition), Bava Batra 5:38","assessment":"Direct Glick edition comparison verifies the Yitzhak variant three times in the final unit on the passage. The Bavli keeps Huna. Apply this exact link to the alternative, separate from the Bavli anchor.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ein Yaakov (Glick Edition), Bava Batra 5:38","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ein_Yaakov_%28Glick_Edition%29%2C_Bava_Batra_5.38"},"witness":"En Jacob, translated by SH Glick, 1916"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 91a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_91a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"holds":[{"raw":"תלמיד רב","reason":"Four sources explicitly transmit in Rav’s name. This does not independently establish personal pupilhood. The assertions of pupilhood and the Rav Yehudah title correction stay attributed to the author.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 71b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_71b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 45b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_45b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ובשס\"ח ר' יהודה ט\"ס","reason":"The named Menahot witness agrees with Rav Yehudah. The specific new-Shas witness and its reported reading remain uncollated.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 26b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_26b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ועיי' רבינא","reason":"The Bavli names Ravina. Heilprin has multiple Ravina notices and does not specify which his pointer targets. The exact Sotah episode is independently linked.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 46b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_46b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The main Bavli preserves both Rabbah and Rava. A direct Glick Ein Yaakov comparison confirms the Yitzhak variant at Bava Batra 91a, while the named Bavli reads Huna. The exact new-Shas witness and the biographical inference of personal pupilhood remain qualified.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 71b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_71b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 45b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_45b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
